      "summary": "Enhance | FORGE Methodology | Embracing Digital Embracing Digital Home Guidance Briefings (EDTW) What changed Interviews (EDT) How others did it Architectural Deep Dives What to do next Learn Digital Transformation Overview Pillars AI, Cyber, Data, Edge, Computing, Comms ODXA Domains &amp; mappings Whitepapers Monthly synthesis Articles Explainers &amp; analysis Lectures (DTA) Learning series Community Community Newsletter Patreon LinkedIn About About Host Sponsors Shop Search Enhance Scale and Optimize The Architect's Explosion The Enhance stage is the scaling, optimization, and innovation phase of the FORGE methodology within the GEAR framework. Building upon grounded foundations and reconciled architectures, it drives continuous capability expansion through advanced automation, modern execution pillars, and optimized workflows across the transformation dimensions. This phase delivers compounding mission value by iterating rapidly on user feedback, integrating emerging technologies, and sustaining long-term organizational agility. Augment Capabilities Introduce the strategic technologies and processes identified in the earlier stages. This is where the Execution Pillars (AI, Cyber, Data, etc.) are fully integrated. Strategic Optimization Move from \"functional\" to \"optimal.\" Refine workflows and system configurations to maximize mission value and efficiency. Scale and Sustain Prepare the new capabilities for enterprise-wide scaling. Establish the patterns and practices that will ensure the transformation is sustainable over the long term. Key Activities Advanced Feature Rollout: Deploy the full suite of transformed digital and physical capabilities. Process Re-engineering: Implement the optimized workflows reconciled in stage 3. Capability Scaling: Move successful pilots into full production across the enterprise. Feedback Loop Integration: Establish the monitoring and feedback mechanisms that will trigger the next \"Find\" stage as the enterprise evolves. Previous: ",
